The keys of the cert\-authority lines, up to CAP of them, for the trusted_user_cas of the authentication machine.  Returns the number of them (which may be more than CAP).  Owned by the table.
.TP
int \fBgf_authkeys_check\fP (const gf_authkeys *t, const gf_auth_request *req, const char *address, const char *hostname, uint64_t now, gf_authkey_match *match);
Is the request's key authorized for the request's user?  REQ is a GF_AUTH_PUBLICKEY request.  ADDRESS is the client's address in text and HOSTNAME its name, either of them NULL if unknown; NOW is wall time in seconds since 1970.  Returns 1 with *MATCH set (if not NULL) for the first line that authorizes it, 0 if none does, or a negative status for a bad argument.  Whether the key is acceptable at all, what its signature says and the rest of auth.h's checks have been done by the machine.
.TP
int \fBgf_authkey_permits\fP (const gf_authkey_match *m, const char *permission);
Does the line allow PERMISSION, one of the GF_CERT_PERMIT_* names of key.h?  Any other name is not allowed.
.TP
int \fBgf_authkey_permits_open\fP (const gf_authkey_match *m, const char *host, unsigned port);
May the user be given a direct\-tcpip channel to HOST:PORT (host names compared without regard to case)?  1 if the line has no permitopen.
.TP
int \fBgf_authkey_permits_listen\fP (const gf_authkey_match *m, const char *host, unsigned port);
May the user ask for a remote forward to listen on HOST:PORT (HOST is the address in the tcpip\-forward request, "" or NULL for the default)?  1 if the line has no permitlisten.
.TP
int \fBgf_authkey_permits_open_path\fP (const gf_authkey_match *m);
.br
int \fBgf_authkey_permits_listen_path\fP (const gf_authkey_match *m);
May the user be given a direct\-streamlocal channel to a Unix socket, or listen on one (streamlocal\-forward)?  A path cannot be named by permitopen or permitlisten, which OpenSSH leaves to the permission of port forwarding (gf_authkey_permits), but a user who was restricted to some hosts and ports should not get at any socket of the machine either: so these are 1 only for a line with no permitopen (open) or no permitlisten (listen).  A server also asks gf_authkey_permits for "permit\-port\-forwarding", and decides which paths it allows.
.TP
int \fBgf_authkey_next\fP (const gf_authkey_match *m, enum gf_authkey_list which, size_t *pos, gf_slice *item);
The values of a repeated option of the line, in order: start with *POS = 0; each call returns 1 and sets ITEM (not NUL\-terminated; valid while the table is), or 0 at the end.
